.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_review-results-12.md:5:Round-11 blocking gaps are closed. The live Ed25519 fixture authenticates through the opaque SSHPublicKeyCredential signer callback, proves host-policy-before-credential ordering, uses only the opaque keychain.fixture.ed25519 reference at the transport seam, exercises exec, and returns all owned resources to zero. Deterministic protected-byte and injected-time threshold tests reach the production libssh2 KEX path under active channels, emit typed trigger/success evidence, increment the matching mandatory counters, preserve post-KEX traffic, and return resources to baseline.
