.resources/TASK-260715-2nfz7w/TASK-260715-2nfz7w_boundaries.md:4:- ReluxTunnelCore (SPM library): pure Swift, NO NetworkExtension or platform-only imports. Owns tunnel runtime contracts; the SSHTransport protocol (connect / openDirectTCPIP / openExecChannel / upload — ssh-transport.md; keep the engine INJECTABLE, do NOT pick ReluxNIOSSH vs libssh2 here — that is TASK-260715-1gjxer); the packet-bridge interface (public packetFlow <-> bridge, no utun-FD discovery — ADR-003); the internal-SOCKS component boundary (not a user proxy); and the platform-adapter seam.
.resources/TASK-260715-2nfz7w/TASK-260715-2nfz7w_boundaries.md-5-- Platform adapter modules (named, thin): the ONLY place NetworkExtension is imported. iOS and macOS composition roots adapt NEPacketTunnelProvider lifecycle + NEPacketTunnelFlow to the shared contracts. The concrete NEPacketTunnelProvider subclasses are LATER tasks (3dv8ea macOS, 2hiabd iOS) and the signed extension targets are gated behind Gate A0/P0. So HERE: define the adapter PROTOCOL + a testable composition root, and prove BOTH adapters satisfy the shared contract via Swift Testing contract tests with the NE surface abstracted/mocked. Do NOT require the generated Xcode workspace.
.resources/TASK-260715-2nfz7w/TASK-260715-2nfz7w_boundaries.md-6-- Dependency direction: core must NOT reach into containing apps or generated target state; enforce + document (a build/test check is ideal).
