.resources/TASK-260720-3vwls7/TASK-260720-3vwls7_inputs.md:1:Fork pinned libssh2 (commit a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719, BSD-3-Clause; OpenSSL 3.5.7 backend) to export a PUBLIC client-initiated rekey. libssh2 ALREADY does KEX re-exchange for server-initiated rekey (src/packet.c -> ssh2_kex_exchange(session,1,...)); ssh2_kex_exchange is defined in src/kex.c but declared only in private src/libssh2_priv.h. ADD a minimal public wrapper (e.g. libssh2_session_rekey in include/libssh2.h) that invokes the existing client re-exchange path (reexchange=1) and returns nonblocking-friendly status (EAGAIN-driven). This is the libssh2 analogue of the NIOSSH _rekey() fork (nzdzv3) and is anticipated by ADR-019 (libssh2 is a locally-rebuilt static XCFramework C dep). Package via the TASK-260715-1g9cyt seam (checksum-verify pinned source BEFORE patching; mismatch fails closed; rebuild XCFramework; preserve extension-safety static gates). Keep the delta MINIMAL + allowlisted, document a PATCH_MANIFEST + delta/rebase doc, preserve BSD-3-Clause + OpenSSL notices, do NOT change crypto/algorithms. Add a deterministic test proving a client-initiated rekey completes and re-establishes keys, and that server-initiated rekey still works. Concrete libssh2/OpenSSL symbols stay inside the fork/adapter boundary (make validate-core enforces no leak into ReluxTunnelCore). If exporting client rekey needs more than a bounded wrapper, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact delta + a viability note for TASK-260715-1gjxer.
.resources/TASK-260720-3vwls7/TASK-260720-3vwls7_results.md:1:Public libssh2_session_rekey wrapper added as one allowlisted two-file patch over pin a343024. The static five-architecture ReluxLibSSH2 XCFramework was rebuilt reproducibly with OpenSSL 3.5.7 after pre-patch archive verification. Deterministic OpenSSH integration evidence shows client-initiated and server-initiated NEWKEYS installation with post-rekey channels. Verification passed: make validate-libssh2; make test-libssh2-source-gates; Swift public-module packaging test; native dependency tests; strict Swift format; make validate-core with 62 tests and swift build.
