EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-lkshfz_ssh-engine-spike/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_integrate-libssh2-candidate-adapter/README.md:4:Implement the libssh2 candidate adapter behind the revised M0-viability SSH transport contract, including nonblocking socket integration and bounded async adaptation, and build it in the macOS harness and the macOS provider configuration. libssh2 is the human-approved primary candidate (2026-07-28). The four semantics deferred to M3 are surfaced as explicit not-reported or unsupported states, never fabricated values, and never silent fallbacks.
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-lkshfz_ssh-engine-spike/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_integrate-libssh2-candidate-adapter/README.md-5-
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-lkshfz_ssh-engine-spike/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_integrate-libssh2-candidate-adapter/README.md-6-## Scope
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-lkshfz_ssh-engine-spike/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_integrate-libssh2-candidate-adapter/README.md:7:In scope: pinned libssh2 and crypto backend; extension-safe static or source build; session handshake; raw host-key access before authentication; approved public-key auth; direct-tcpip; bidirectional exec and exec/stdin upload; client-initiated rekey trigger; nonblocking EAGAIN integration; bounded buffers; deterministic cancellation and timeouts; keepalive; cheaply-available metrics; privacy-safe error mapping; allocator hooks where supported; macOS harness registration; macOS provider configuration build. Out of scope: iOS simulator and iPhone provider configurations (iOS deferred); consumer-driven receive-window credit semantics, RFC channel-open reason taxonomy, exact exec-exit metadata, and deep rekey/keepalive observability (all owned by the M3 task); NIOSSH fork work; masking an unsupported viability gate without a recorded decision; blocking calls on provider executors; SFTP; password prompts; ProxyJump; agent forwarding; production lane scheduling; candidate types outside the adapter.
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-lkshfz_ssh-engine-spike/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_integrate-libssh2-candidate-adapter/README.md-8-
