EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-lkshfz_ssh-engine-spike/TASK-260720-100wu6_implement-candidate-neutral-ssh-transport-contract/README.md:10:1. ReluxTunnelCore exposes the complete reviewed candidate-neutral interface without importing or naming ReluxNIOSSH, SwiftNIO, libssh2, OpenSSL, or adapter types. 2. The type and dependency shape makes raw host-key bytes, algorithm, and SHA-256 fingerprint policy input before credential access or authentication, and represents every required host/auth outcome. 3. Direct-tcpip and exec channels expose bounded partial writes, reads, stdout/stderr and exit results, EOF and half-close, reset, cancel, idempotent close, exec-stdin upload, and independently observable capped receive windows. 4. Injected clock and policy types expose automatic byte/time rekey, explicit production-path trigger, server rekey, keepalive, cancellation/timeouts, typed events, and schema-v1 privacy-safe metrics exactly as the reviewed contract defines. 5. Swift Testing fixtures verify invalid states and policy validation, candidate-type erasure, stable error mapping/data shape, metric/event schema, and secret/destination/command exclusion; the package boundary checks and core build pass.
