+# TASK-260715-1gjxer — solution-architect handoff evidence
+
+## Outcome
+
+Recorded the binding ADR-014 selection of libssh2 for M0 and preserved
+ReluxNIOSSH as explicit comparative `FAIL` / `NOT RUN` evidence. Every accepted
+M0 mandatory gate maps to row-level evidence for both candidates. The selected
+engine has no waived red or unexecuted M0 gate.
+
+The ADR includes exact libssh2/OpenSSL/fork and retained ReluxNIOSSH pins,
+license/notice duties, the adapter boundary, approved algorithms, injectable
+window and rekey domains, maintenance and security-monitoring obligations,
+fork/rebase ownership, residual risks, revalidation triggers, rejected evidence,
+the four M3 semantics, physical evidence still owed, and M1/M2 readiness.
+
+No new board element or dependency was created: the existing decomposition
+already provides atomic evidence producers, one selection task, explicit M3
+owners, and downstream links. No diagram was produced because the decision is a
+gate/evidence matrix rather than a topology ambiguity.
+
+## Fresh controlled selected-engine evidence
+
+On source `2064698ca526260d9994582852486301bb06a752`, the initial build plus real
+OpenSSH M0 lifecycle test exited 0. Five subsequent already-built runs of
+`swift test --skip-build --filter successfulM0FlowsAndLifecycleBaseline` all
+exited 0. Test-body durations were 11.058–11.144 s. The maximum whole-command
+RSS was 71,254,016 B and maximum macOS peak footprint was 17,891,952 B. Every
+one of three lifecycle iterations per run asserted exact selected-adapter zero
+ownership: no channels, socket, session, automatic task, custom allocation, or
+buffered byte.
+
+This is explicitly a controlled macOS-harness whole-cycle envelope containing
+real `direct-tcpip`, not an isolated DNS channel-open p99, physical extension
+footprint, production DNS authorization, or M3 scale/memory claim.
+
+## Evidence authorities
+
+- Human decision: `TASK-260715-1gjxer_approved-m0-viability-decision.md`.
+- M0 contract: `TASK-260728-yx2fca_ssh-transport-conformance-contract.md`.
+- Selected adapter: accepted `TASK-260715-1ozsb6` and reviewer round 12.
+- Selected matrix: accepted `TASK-260715-1u2vpc` and reviewer verdict.
+- Common conformance: accepted `TASK-260715-2d3g5e` and reviewer verdict.
+- Fixtures/real-host reachability: accepted `TASK-260715-39xz9g`.
+- Candidate audit and pins: accepted `TASK-260715-28ok1k`.
+- Retained NIOSSH fork/blockers: `TASK-260715-nzdzv3` and
+  `TASK-260715-1af33i` outcomes.
+- M3/DNS separation: the two task preconditions supplied with this assignment.
+
+## Validation summary
+
+- First current-tree build and focused M0 lifecycle: exit 0; one real OpenSSH
+  test passed in 11.089 s.
+- Five already-built focused M0 lifecycle runs: 5/5 exit 0.
+- Repository/board validation results are recorded after final artifact
+  attachment; any nonzero exit remains nonzero in this handoff.
+
+## Disposition
+
+The task is ready for independent solution-architect review. `to-review` is the
+role handoff state, not accepted completion. Physical scale, memory, DNS
+footprint, deep observability, and release approval remain outside this handoff.
